PU Workspace third-party notices
================================

PU Workspace includes or is built with third-party software. Copyright and
license rights in those components belong to their respective owners.

The authoritative technical inventory for a delivery is the three SPDX 2.3
files generated by `scripts/legal_release_kit.py sbom`, together with
`third-party-license-matrix.json`, `license-evidence.json`,
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` and `ASSET_PROVENANCE.md`. The accompanying
`docs/legal/06_THIRD_PARTY_COMPONENTS_RU.md` is the human-readable review sheet.

No third-party trademark, hosted service, account, dataset, font, image or
logo is transferred merely because its name appears in documentation or code.
Google, Telegram, PostgreSQL, Docker and AI-provider services are separately
licensed/contracted by the buyer unless a signed specification says otherwise.

RELEASE GATE: package-declared license metadata is evidence, not a legal
conclusion. Before external delivery, approve every `licenseConcluded`, resolve
each documented gap, lock the complete Python/container graph, collect every
package-specific license/notice file, fill the right holder in LICENSE, and
have the result reviewed. This repository-level NOTICE is not a substitute for
component license texts or the right holder's signed license terms.

The generated THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md now contains a package-specific evidence
index (component, exact version, declared license, public evidence URL and
metadata SHA-256). It still does not replace the upstream LICENSE/COPYING/NOTICE
texts, which remain a release gate until collected and reviewed.
